{
  "$schema": "../../schema/incident.schema.json",
  "protocol": "MEV bot 0x03f911ae",
  "name": "MEV bot 0x03f911ae pays uniswapV3SwapCallback to any caller",
  "summary": "The bot's uniswapV3SwapCallback(amount0Delta, amount1Delta, data) transfers the owed token from the bot's own balance to msg.sender without checking that the caller is a Uniswap V3 pool, so any contract can call it with a positive delta and receive that token. The anchor's contract 0x6c6b87d4 called it for 3,066.79 TAMA and sold them for 0.0112 WETH. Over the next four years at least 41 more transactions (searcher contracts, EOAs calling the callback directly, and calls that had the bot swap against a fake pool that then called back) took tokens the bot held, the largest 338,324 imgnAI sold for 4.04 WETH in June 2023 and the DeFiHackLabs transaction's 0.737 WETH in September 2024.",
