  "notes": [
    "Mechanism from traces, as the bot is unverified. Victim is the bot's operator (deployer 0xc82ea2af); the bot's only direct transactions besides its creation are direct callback calls by unrelated EOAs, which are exploits too.",
    "Exploits found from all 379,441 token Transfer events out of the bot from its deployment to the chain head: every recipient was classified by its factory() (Uniswap V3 0x1f98431c and PancakeSwap V3 0xbaceb8ec pools are normal swaps), and each transaction paying a non-pool recipient a non-zero amount was traced; all but two (which paid a V2 pair without a callback) ran the callback from a non-pool. The earliest is the anchor, five months after deployment; the bot's code never changed (direct deployment).",
    "Loss is the bot's token outflow in the 42 transactions (loss.mjs, nets the WETH the bot got back in the same transaction). Tokens without a DefiLlama price are valued at the WETH the taker received for them in the same transaction at hourly ETH prices (rule 12): imgnAI 4.0419 WETH ($6,739.61), and 14 more for $167 together; MORSE, ENTC and 4GatosCoin were never sold and count 0. Native ETH the bot may have lost is not covered by the Transfer scan.",
    "The DeFiHackLabs transaction 0x1a3e9eb5 (0xf073a21f via 0xd683b81c) is in the campaign; the same attacker had already taken four tokens in August 2024 and took WETH again in December 2024 and January 2025. c0ffeebabe's eight transactions are counted at their gross outflow: its contracts also sent the bot 1,869 WSM just before its WSM drains and 381 USDT in 2026, which are separate transactions and not netted (rule 11)."
  ]
